Determination of anthocyanin chlorophyll and carotenoid contents
The anthocyanin content was determined by Serrano’s method [
32
]. The entire test for anthocyanin content determination needs to be carried out in the dark and at low temperature. Weigh 2 g of fresh sample tissue and grind it in liquid nitrogen. Place the tissue sample in a 25 ml centrifuge tube, add 6 ml of 1% hydrochloric acid - methanol solution pre-cooled at 4℃, mix thoroughly, and shake at 4℃ in the dark for 24 h. After the tissue sample turns white, let it stand for 15 min, and centrifuge at 12,000 g at room temperature for 10 min. Draw the supernatant and pour it into the cuvette. Use a UV-Vis spectrophotometer (UV-1800pc, MAPADA, Shanghai, China) to read the absorbance values at 530 nm and 657 nm in the visible light region. Repeat this biological process three times. Calculate the anthocyanin content according to the formula:
